Numerical determination of the local dimension of a solution of a =20
polynomial system

Dan Bates

Colorado State University, Fort Collins CO

  A new symbolic-numerical local dimension test.
  One of the sticky problems in numerical algebraic geometry over
  the years has been determining the local dimension of a solution p =20
of a
  polynomial system F.  The local dimension is just the maximum =20
dimension of
  the irreducible components on which p sits.  This new is a hybrid
  symbolic-numerical method that detects the dimension of _all_ =20
components
  containing p by computing ranks of various matrices (formed from =20
taking
  higher and higher partial derivatives of the system, more or less).  =20=

This
  is joint work with J. Hauenstein, C. Peterson, and A. Sommese.

