Computation modulo regular chains

Wei Pan

The University of Western Ontario. London, Canada

  The computation of triangular decompositions of polynomial systems =20
is based on two fundamental operations:
  polynomial GCDs modulo regular chains  and regularity test modulo =20
saturated ideals.

  We propose new algorithms for these core operations relying on =20
modular methods and fast polynomial arithmetic.
  Our strategies take also advantage of the context in which these =20
operations are performed.

  We report on extensive experimentation, comparing our code to pre-=20
existing Maple implementations, as well
  as more optimized Magma functions. In most cases, our new code =20
outperforms the other packages by several
  orders of magnitude.=09

